  "implementation": [
    "Existing TLS C/OpenSSL implementation reused with matching public record layouts and private allocation prefixes. Last release disposes factory resources; default records preserve stdin; stream string fields are freed once.",
    "Registry limits remain 1024 streams / 256 listeners. Registry access and once initialization are serialized. Existing TLS process SIGPIPE policy is preserved.",
    "No value copy hook is invented; legacy native TLS value copies lack a hook too."
  ],
  "independent_controls": [
    "C archive and Rust FFI clients cover binary NUL/high bytes, UTF8 lines, snapshots, alias credits, concurrent factories, default/nil records, fd closure, portable shutdown wakeup and accepted stream lifetime after listener release.",
    "Ephemeral localhost-only certificates are generated with linked OpenSSL. Trusted loopback succeeds; untrusted certificate and hostname mismatch reject through the same C error contract. System trust is unchanged.",
    "Original external test source, example.com endpoint, certificate verification and oracle stay unchanged across nine C/Rust modes."
  ],
